---
title: "Case Studies: Production AI & Data Engineering | ByteStreams"
description: "Case studies from ByteStreams: production AI and data engineering for healthcare organizations and growing companies, with the problem, approach and results."
keywords: "AI case studies, data engineering case study, healthcare AI case study, data platform modernization, production AI systems, ByteStreams"
# Paginating over the collection means this page is only built once at least
# one non-draft case study exists — no empty index ever ships.
pagination:
  data: collections.caseStudies
  size: 50
  alias: studies
permalink: "/case-studies/"
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>{% include "head.njk" %}</head>
<body data-theme="dark">

{% include "header.njk" %}

<main id="main">

    <section class="blog-hero">
        <div class="blog-hero__container">
            <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
                <ol class="breadcrumb__list">
                    <li class="breadcrumb__item"><a href="/" class="breadcrumb__link">Home</a></li>
                    <li class="breadcrumb__item" aria-current="page">Case Studies</li>
                </ol>
            </nav>
            <h1 class="blog-hero__title">Case Studies</h1>
            <p class="blog-hero__subtitle">
                Production AI and data engineering case studies: the problem, how we built it, and what changed.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="blog-listing section">
        <div class="section__container">
            <div class="blog-grid">
                {% for study in studies %}
                <article class="post-card">
                    <div class="post-card__meta">
                        {% if study.data.industry %}
                        <span class="post-card__tag">{{ study.data.industry }}</span>
                        {% endif %}
                    </div>
                    <h2 class="post-card__title">
                        <a href="{{ study.url }}" class="post-card__link">{{ study.data.headline or study.data.title }}</a>
                    </h2>
                    <p class="post-card__excerpt">{{ study.data.description }}</p>
                    <div class="post-card__footer">
                        <a href="{{ study.url }}" class="post-card__cta" aria-label="Read case study: {{ study.data.headline or study.data.title }}">
                            Read case study <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-right" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                        </a>
                    </div>
                </article>
                {% endfor %}
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

</main>

{% include "footer.njk" %}

<script src="/js/main.js" defer></script>
</body>
</html>
